    <baseline year="2022">
     <comment>
      <narrative xml:lang="EN">No data on feasibility of the viable and gender sensitive and inclusive finance mechanisms on funding Yashil Makon;

There is no a long-term integrated master plan for forest landscape restoration and greening initiative for Uzbekistan across regions;

No coordination mechanism of Yashil Makon implementation by various partners;    

No urban/rural greening action plans with clear targets;

No digital solutions on forest landscape restoration.</narrative>
     </comment>
    </baseline>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2022-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2022-12-31"></period-end>
     <target>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">3.1. 600 Afghan citizens and 400 local poor women and young people (m/f) engaged in the economic activities on planting in Surkhandarya province.</narrative>
      </comment>
     </target>
     <actual>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">3.1. 100 ha land in Termez city and three districts &#x2013; Termez, Sherabad, Djarkurgan was planted involving erosion control plantations and forest-forming species. In the reporting period in total 625 persons (91 women), including 448 Afghan citizens (56 women) residing in Surkhandarya have been registered and involved to the planting activities in Termez city, Termez and Sherobod Districts.</narrative>
      </comment>
     </actual>
    </period>
   </indicator>
